# Tree

One tree for this project. Same folder names everywhere; a folder can be thin or empty, but don't invent new top-level ones.

```
<project>/
  public/          docroot ONLY: index.php (front controller), .htaccess, assets/, robots.txt, ads.txt, sitemap
  config/          routes.php, site.php, SEO/ads registries, env.php (secrets, gitignored), env.example.php
  core/            shared Router, Controller, App — copied from shared-core-ref
  controllers/     thin request handlers
  services/        logic / use cases
  models/          only when there's a DB
  views/           layouts/, partials/, <page>/ templates
  migrations/      only when there's a DB
  bin/             CLI scripts
  tests/
  docs/
  .cursor/rules/   00–07 shared (reinstall via install-rules.sh) + 10-<project>.mdc
  composer.json    PSR-4 autoload
```

## Where things live

- DocumentRoot is always `<repo>/public/`.
- Local dev: `http://gpstoolset.lan/`. Use that URL to test, never `localhost/<path>`.
- Production: `https://gpstoolset.com/` behind Cloudflare when live.
- Never hard-code `/var/www/...` or a domain in code: use `__DIR__`-based paths and `site.php` / `Env` base URL.

