## Env and secrets (decided 2026-11-05)

- Location: `config/env.php` in every repo. It returns a PHP array, is gitignored, and is never inside `public/`.
- `config/env.example.php` is committed with the same keys and fake values. Add a key there whenever you add one to env.php.
- Access: only through `Core\Env` (`core/Env.php`): `Env::get('KEY', $default)` or `Env::require('KEY')`. No direct `getenv()`, `$_ENV`, or `require 'env.php'` anywhere else.
- Order: server env (`$_SERVER`, e.g. Apache `SetEnv`) > `getenv()` > `config/env.php` > default.
- Standard keys: `APP_ENV` (dev|prod), `BASE_URL`, and `DB_HOST`/`DB_NAME`/`DB_USER`/`DB_PASS` when there's a DB. Project keys get a prefix (e.g. `GPS_`, `PS_`).
- `.gitignore` in every repo: `config/env.php`, `config/*.local.php`, `*.env`, `.env*` (keep examples).
- Never print, log or commit a secret value. Never expose env values to JS unless they're public (e.g. GA4 ID).
- Migrate any legacy secrets into `config/env.php` and read them only through `Core\Env`.

## Router and views (CI3-style) — core-ref 1.1.3-draft

- All requests go through `public/index.php`; `.htaccess` rewrites anything that isn't a real file.
- `config/routes.php` returns `['route' => $route, 'redirect' => $redirect]`:
  - `$route['default_controller']`, `$route['404_override']`, `$route['auto_route'] = false` (default)
  - Explicit: `$route['privacy'] = 'pages/privacy'` (any method) or `$route['api/x']['post'] = 'api/x'` (verb; HEAD≡GET; else 405)
  - Placeholders `(:any)` / `(:num)` → `$1`, `$2`
  - `$redirect['old.php'] = 'new'` — 301 before routes; supports `(:any)`/`$1` and absolute URLs; keeps query string
- Trailing slash: `/x/` → 301 `/x` (not `/`); query string kept.
- `auto_route` false → only listed routes + `/`. True → `controller/method/args`, never `_…` or base `Controller` methods.
- 404: missing class/method/route or `$this->notFound()` → `404_override` with HTTP 404; if that fails → plain 404.
- Controllers: `$this->view('page/name', $data)`, `$this->input` (`Input`: get/post/server/method/isPost/isAjax/json/ip/uri/segment — strings raw; views use `e()`), `$this->notFound()`.
- Shared partials: head, seo, analytics, consent, ads, header, footer.
- Core copy-in from `shared-core-ref` 1.1.3-draft (`Core\`, `App\Controllers\` PSR-4).
